also":"","summary":"Useful, a slave who, after robbing his master Philemon at Colosse, fled to Rome, where he was converted by the apostle Paul, who sent him back to his master with the epistle which bears his name.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[9]},{"id":"barnabas_1722","name":"Barnabas","also":"Jupiter, Joses","summary":"Son of consolation, the surname of Joses, a Levite (Acts 4:36). His name stands first on the list of prophets and teachers of the church at Antioch (13:1).","verses":29,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"mark_1679","name":"John","also":"Marcus","summary":"The evangelist; “John whose surname was Mark” (Acts 12:12, 25). Mark (Marcus, Col. 4:10, etc.) was his Roman name, which gradually came to supersede his Jewish name John.","verses":10,"father":"","mother":"Mary","v":[10]},{"id":"aristarchus_306","name":"Aristarchus","also":"","summary":"Best ruler, native of Thessalonica (Acts 20:4), a companion of Paul (Acts 19:29; 27:2).","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[10]},{"id":"jesus_904","name":"Jesus","also":"","summary":"A Jewish Christian surnamed Justus (Col. 4:11).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"epaphras_1195","name":"Epaphras","also":"","summary":"Lovely, spoken of by Paul (Col. 1:7; 4:12) as “his dear fellow-servant,” and “a faithful minister of Christ.” He was thus evidently with him at Rome when he wrote to the Colossians.","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[12]},{"id":"demas_1006","name":"Demas","also":"","summary":"A companion and fellow-labourer of Paul during his first imprisonment at Rome (Philemon 1:24; Col. 4:14).","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"luke_1836","name":"Luke","also":"Lucas","summary":"The evangelist, was a Gentile. The date and circumstances of his conversion are unknown. According to his own statement (Luke 1:2), he was not an “eye-witness and minister of the word from the beginning.”","verses":3,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"archippus_292","name":"Archippus","also":"","summary":"Master of the horse, a “fellow-soldier” of Paul’s (Philemon 1:2), whom he exhorts to renewed activity (Col. 4:17).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[17]},{"id":"paul_2479","name":"Paul","also":"Saul, Mercurius","summary":"Saul was born about the same time as our Lord. His circumcision-name was Saul, and probably the name Paul was also given to him in infancy “for use in the Gentile world,” as “Saul” would be his Hebrew home-name.","verses":179,"father":"","mother":"","v":[18]}],"places":[{"id":"hierapolis_569","name":"Hierapolis","kind":"City","lat":37.92452,"lon":29.12452,"summary":"Sacred city, a city of Phrygia, where was a Christian church under the care of Epaphras (Col. 4:12, 13). This church was founded at the same time as that of Colosse.","verses":1,"v":[13]},{"id":"laodicea_716","name":"Laodicea","kind":"City","lat":37.83692,"lon":29.10786,"summary":"The city of this name mentioned in Scripture lay on the confines of Phrygia and Lydia, about 40 miles east of Ephesus (Rev. 3:14), on the banks of the Lycus.","verses":6,"v":[13,15,16]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["Barnes","JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[2962,3930,3588,1401,3588,3588,1342,1342,2532,2471,1492,1492,1492,3754,4771,2532,2192,2962,2962,1722,3772],[4342,4342,3588,4335,1127,1127,1722,2169],[260,4336,4336,2532,4012,1473,2443,2316,455,455,1473,1473,2374,2374,3588,3588,3056,2980,2980,2980,2980,2980,3588,3466,5547,5547,1223,3739,1210,1210,1210,1210],[2443,2443,5319,5319,5319,5319,5319,5613,1473,1163],[4043,4678,4314,1854,1805,3588,2540],[4771,4771,3056,3842,3842,5485,741,217,217,1492,1492,1492,1492,1492,4459,611,611,1538],[5190,1107,1107,4771,3956,3588,3588,2596,1473,3588,3588,27,27,80,4103,4103,1249,2532,4889,4889,4889,1722,2962,2962],[3992,3992,3992,3739,4314,4771,1519,846,846,3778,2443,1097,1097,1097,4012,1473,2532,2532,3870,3870,3870,4771,2588],[4862,4862,4862,4862,4862,3682,3588,4103,2532,27,80,3739,1510,1537,1537,4771,1107,1107,1107,4771,